predicate.note:
Round 2, the meaning of `from`. C12 gives one parameter three meanings, chosen by which other parameter is present:
- a record id, in listings;
- a 1-based extent index, when `id` is given;
- "the same from" for `deps`.

`deps` always carries an `id`, so by C12's own rule its `from` is an extent index, yet what deps pages is dependent ids. The two rules collide exactly there. A claim has no extents, so "its extents page the same way" is undefined for `id`=C#. The listing's trailer for a record whose surplus extents were counted names only the next record, so nothing routes the reader to `id`+`from`=index to recover those extents.

Two coherent alternatives:
- split the parameter, e.g. `from` for records and a separate extent offset;
- or make every `from` an opaque token that the trailer hands back.

Changes only what the implementer is told: the parameter surface, which the CLI flags mirror.
